Two parts of the operations request are not implemented:

1. **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the component targets `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, and no filesystem or logging capability is in its world. There is no import it could write through.
2. **Fetching `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=<input text>`:** the node holds `HTTPClient<['feeds.example.com']>`. A request to another host is a trap at the boundary. It would also send the input text to a service outside the node's grant.

If either is needed, the graph should give the node a logging capability or a wider HTTP allowlist.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{heartbeat-report};

    import aap:caps/http-client@0.1.0;
    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;
    import wasi:clocks/wall-clock@0.2.0;

    export run: func(feed-url: string) -> heartbeat-report;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(feed_url: String) -> HeartbeatReport {
        let seconds = crate::wasi::clocks::wall_clock::now().seconds;

        let fetched = match crate::aap::caps::http_client::fetch(&feed_url) {
            Ok(body) => body.chars().count() as u32,
            Err(_) => 0,
        };

        let message = format!("heartbeat at {} fetched {}", seconds, fetched);

        // The contract requires notified == true, so retry a refused notification.
        let mut notified = false;
        for _ in 0..3 {
            if crate::aap::caps::notifier::notify(&message) {
                notified = true;
                break;
            }
        }

        HeartbeatReport {
            seconds,
            fetched,
            notified,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

